  "primary_subject_agency_ids": [],
  "summary": "Florida Governor Ron DeSantis ordered Flock automated license plate reader cameras removed from the state highway system within 30 days, citing concerns about misuse and surveillance. The Florida Department of Transportation memo says it will deny future permits for such cameras, and DeSantis called for a legislative solution next spring since the order could be reversed by a future governor.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "On Monday, DeSantis ordered all Flock cameras removed from what he calls the \"state highway system\" within the next 30 days, which would include interstates like I-10 and I-75.",
      "paragraph_idx": 6
    },
    {
      "quote": "That order led to several sheriff's departments like in Franklin, Liberty and Putnam Counties to announce they're ending their own license plate reader programs.",
      "paragraph_idx": 6
    },
    {
      "quote": "We know there was an officer in Florida who was using the LPR data to track like an ex-girlfriend or something like that",
      "paragraph_idx": 10
    }
  ],
